multiflexi-mcp-server (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Revert 0.3.0's MULTIFLEXI_HOST/USERNAME/PASSWORD defaults
    (https://demo.multiflexi.eu/api + demo/demo credentials): a
    zero-config install that silently talks to a public shared demo
    backend is a security footgun (easy to forget to override before
    pointing a real deployment at it, and it normalizes shipping
    credentials in defaults). The server now refuses to start with a
    clear RuntimeError if MULTIFLEXI_HOST is unset, and no longer
    defaults USERNAME/PASSWORD to "demo"/"demo".
  * .env.example/README: document that MULTIFLEXI_HOST must include the
    full API base path (.../api/VitexSoftware/MultiFlexi/1.0.0), which is
    required by the server's routing, not optional boilerplate.
  * Add MULTIFLEXI_READONLY (default: true). When enabled, all mutating
    tools (create_job, update_runtemplate, request_data_export,
    assign_user_to_company, unassign_user_from_company, set_user_roles,
    update_credential, update_credential_type, update_topic,
    set_event_source, delete_event_source, set_event_rule,
    delete_event_rule) are rejected before any API call is made. Set to
    false to allow writes.

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200

multiflexi-mcp-server (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix server version reported in the MCP handshake drifting from the
    package version (now read via importlib.metadata instead of a
    hardcoded string).
  * Fix default MULTIFLEXI_HOST pointing at a non-functional SwaggerHub
    mock server instead of the documented public demo server; now
    defaults to https://demo.multiflexi.eu/api with demo/demo
    credentials so a zero-config install works out of the box.
  * Add MCP prompts capability: diagnose_job_failure,
    task_fulfillment_report, gdpr_export_checklist.
  * Add SKILL.md describing a MultiFlexi operations skill.

 -- Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Sat, 08 Aug 2026 18:00:00 +0200

multiflexi-mcp-server (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Lazily import multiflexi_client in client.py to fix ~5s cold-start
    import time causing intermittent MCP handshake-timeout failures;
    bump upstream to 0.2.0 to cut accumulated Unreleased changes
    (update_credential/update_credential_type/update_topic tools,
    Pydantic v2 fixes, job/status endpoint corrections).

